last night I saw something that I never  thought I would ever see on American  soil it was the stuff of tin-pot  dictator Zin banana republics as you  probably know throughout the entire  country our protests against police  brutality and systemic unfairness and  racism so of course because this is 2020  the thing that was used to fight those  protesting that unfairness and brutality  was yet more unfairness and brutality I  never thought I would ever see anything  like what happened last night in America  what I saw last night was a threat to  our democracy not foreign but domestic a  violation of rights of freedoms and of  laws by the very people who are supposed  to protect and execute those laws  Lafayette Square is a place that I know  very very well  I worked downtown for years and I would  often go to Lafayette Park for a coffee  or to have lunch outside and it's a  beautiful park right in front of the  White House it's also the site of many  protests there are actually protests  there basically 365 days a year there  are people who literally camp out in  tents and given its proximity to the  White House it makes sense as one of the  clear protest sites of choice there have  been protests there for decades if not  literally hundreds of years and while  President Trump was giving a speech  about domination he gave the order to  clear out all of the protesters who were  at and in front of Lafayette Park  President Trump speech began shortly  after 6:00 p.m. he gave the order to  clear out the park at 6:35 p.m. it was a  site of a peaceful protest not all of  these protests have been peaceful but  the one in Lafayette Park was it was  attended by peaceful protesters by the  media as we speak  I am dispatching thousands and thousands  of heavily armed soldiers military  personnel and law enforcement officers  to stop the rioting looting vandalism  assault and the wanton destruction of  property and it's 6:35 p.m. he gave the  order to round everyone up to clear them  out and someone whether it was the  president or those acting under his  orders tear gassed the protesters shot  them with rubber munitions and generally  just beat the [ __ ] out  federal officers armed to the teeth  wearing protective riot gear dressed in  all black clad with plastic shields and  backed up by what was effectively  cavalry on horses began rounding  everyone up and pushing them out this  was the sort of tactic that was designed  to get violent years of study of crowd  control have shown that the way to  de-escalate a situation like this is  effectively to do the exact opposite and  yet these federal officers wearing riot  gear effectively tried to bum rush out  peaceful protesters they came out  swinging literally there's a video  circulating of what one of these federal  officers did to an Australian news crew  after running towards the protesters  this particular officer started punching  and using his shield as a weapon he hits  the Australian cameraman directly in the  stomach beats him up sends him on his  way we have video footage not only of  what one of the protesters saw happening  to this Australian camera crew but also  from the camera crew itself they dealt  with my cameraman team  what was the reason for expelling these  peaceful protesters who were exercising  their constitutional right to protest  the president wanted a photo-op at a  church across the street he wanted to be  able to walk from the White House out  the front door which is rarely done  through Lafayette Park to stand in front  of st. John's Church a nonpartisan place  of worship reports are that little to no  warning was given to the protesters  ahead of time and that it was  coordinated so that he could end his  speech in the Rose Garden and walk  directly out to the church I'm going to  pay my respects to a very very special  place thank you very much  of course when he got to the church for  his photo opportunity he turned his back  on the church he didn't pray he didn't  reflect he didn't even open the Bible he  carried with him he took it out held it  upside down moved it around in different  ways to get the best photo opportunity  stood in front of the church for a  minute or two told the media that it was  a Bible  and then left he cleared out the  protesters before the 7:00 p.m. DC  curfew went into effect and then in the  ultimate irony the president of law and  order stayed past the curfew to get his  photo-op and of course the cherry on top  is that after the crowd was being  dispersed the federal government  employed military Black Hawk helicopters  in a show of force  flying dozens of feet above the crowd in  an incredibly dangerous maneuver that I  can't recall anything like it ever  happening on American soil nothing about  the President's speech or his photo  opportunity was about reconciliation  about progress about repair or even  about amelioration or de-escalation of  the protests it was calculated only to  inflame to make things worse to own the  libs while desecrating a religious site  while blaspheming the Bible and beating  the protesters and we saw the end result  of this callous move this morning just  mere hours after it happened the White  House releases a video montage set to  music the next day a campaign stunt  brought to you by tear gassing some  people like Scott Walker had the  audacity to say that no one else would  have the guts to do what President Trump  did to walk out in front of the crowd  yeah it sure takes a real man to order  other people with guns to fire munitions  at civilians American citizens  exercising their constitutional right to  protest and then walk between a hundred  armed guards and Secret Service members  for a two-minute photo-op after clearing  the area real guts now I've been  referring to these armed guards as  federal officers because all reports  show that these were not DC cops  DC police generally know how to do crowd  control and while we all have issues  with the DC Police Department the  Metropolitan Police Department I'd like  to think that DC cops wouldn't stand for  being puppets of the President so he can  get a photo-op while infringing on  people's constitutional right  apparently the DC police were given  minimal notice they were surprised as  everyone else and one of the ultimate  ironies of this whole situation is that  not only were the DC police totally  uninformed about this maneuver but one  of the priests who is one of the  proprietors of st. John's Church where  the president wanted to have his photo  opportunity was expelled from the area  so the president could stand there mayor  Bowser  the mayor of DC confirmed that nothing  in this particular situation warranted  the use of munitions against the  protesters or the tactics of the riot  police what we saw was before the curfew  time munitions were released on people  who didn't seem to have provoked any  attack and all of the people in this  particular area of DC were in fact  peacefully protesting on this channel I  try to give both sides when there are  both sides to a story there usually are  and in this particular case yes there  were looting and riots in other parts of  the country but they weren't at the  White House no one is supporting the  rioters and the looters but that's not  what was going on here and it could also  be the case that there are bad faith  rioters and protesters and looters who  are part of an otherwise peaceful  protest that's not the issue here the  issue here is that unequivocally  draconian tactics were used on peaceful  protesters before curfew started the  stories about the violent protests and  the unlawful looting and rioting deserve  their own place on the front page of the  New York Times but those stories as of  today deserve to be at the bottom of the  front page because the headline that  should be ringing in every house in  America is that the President of the  United States ordered draconian measures  to expel peaceful protesters so he could  get a photo-op I don't know if it's  possible to overdose on metaphors but  today is actually election day in DC I  don't know something about this whole  situation feels different to me on many  different fronts maybe there are more  cameras out today than in the past and  maybe we're just seeing more of what was  already there and I'm sure that's the  case  but I also wonder if there is more  police abuse that we're seeing as well  when you declare war on America what you  get is a war on America that when you  have federal officers and police dress  up like soldiers they start acting like  soldiers I think in part what we're  seeing today is the result of years of  the president's statements like if you  have a suspect in custody feel free to  rough them up don't be too nice on them  the press is the enemy of the people and  that we need to dominate protesters  making no distinction between looters  and peaceful protesters words have  consequences  the president has a bully pulpit and we  shouldn't be surprised when people  actually follow the words of an  authority figure like the President of  the United States even though I am a  relatively new adopter of the city of  Washington DC as their home I have  adopted it I chose to live here it's my  home and is where I'm gonna stay DC is a  city that has been scarred by the 1968  riots in many ways it's only in the last  say ten years that it's really begun to  heal and I have seen nothing in the last  24 to 48 hours that has done anything to  make things better and the actions that  were taken today threaten that fragile  peace it threatens DC sovereignty as it  were DC is not a state we don't have a  governor often the city can't refuse  federal troops and we don't have the  representatives the senators the  governors and all of the other  privileges that the other states have to  be able to fight the federal government  in the way that they can this is one of  the reasons why DC statehood is so  important  just yesterday morning in those naive  days I was reading an opinion piece by  noted conservative pundit George F will  he wrote in The Washington Post starting  by referring to the president's tweets  about Joe Scarborough stating those who  think are unhinged president's recent  mania about a murder two decades ago  that never happened  represents his moral nadir have missed  the lessons of his life there is no such  thing as rock bottom so assume that the  worst is yet to come I read those words  and I honestly thought that George Will  was overreacting I thought it was a  little histrionic and then of course  because it's 20/20 we all have to eat  our own words and then Lafayette Park  happened yesterday the president said I  am your president of law and order this  is a president who just weeks ago  abdicated all federal responsibilities  regarding kovaydin the coronavirus  calling it a states rights issue and  that the governor should do something  about it and now when it suits him he  aggrandize himself control of all of the  federal officers and the military so  that he can do a photo opportunity if a  city or state refuses to take the  actions that are necessary to defend the  life and property of their residents  then I will deploy the United States  military and quickly solve the problem  for them and he abuses the authority of  the military this is the kind of show of  force that actually escalates into more  violence which is obviously exactly what  some people want now things can and will  get better it might not feel like it but  police shootings nationally are down and  going lower shootings of unarmed people  are going down and accountability is  going up but for things to get better  we're going to have to be proactive  about it and I have to admit that it's  even hard for me an eternal optimist to  be optimistic about the things that I'm  saying on TV  last night today and probably tomorrow  but what can we do  well first record everything if you're  going to take to the streets do so  peacefully and please stop the looters  civil disobedience not only exists to  fight the government itself but also to  fight your fellow men when they're being  unreasonable and if you are going out  please wear masks I really really hope  we're out of the woods with respect to  cope it but this could turn bad we might  have to go into quarantine again  I'm truly conflicted because I think a  lot of this cause is just and it's  fighting injustice but the consequences  are real so please be responsible for  yourself and with respect to other  protesters do what you can to not only  protect them but to protect other  people's property and to record  injustice wherever you see it and to  publish it so that we have at least a  record of it to the members of the armed  citizens who may be asked to turn their  weapons against other American citizens  I ask you to reflect and think about  your actions before you take them that  the highest form of civil disobedience  is to reject an unlawful order and you  may be asked to do so it's not fair but  we all have to play the hands that were  dealt and that unfortunately the federal  military is probably going to be the tip  of the spear on this and the same goes  for the DC Police Department the  Metropolitan Police Department you don't  have to do what we're seeing officers on  TV do there's always a choice and for  everyone else continue speaking out I am  continually astonished by the outpouring  of support that people have given to  this cause and and rightfully so and  we're of course hearing from the usual  suspects it's no surprise the people  that are in support of these things but  there are some groups of people who I  haven't heard from that I would like to  where are all of those Second Amendment  supporters who were so vocal just a  couple of weeks  and who are so silent now when you were  asking for a tyrannical government to  fight against well now is your chance if  you stay at home thinking that the  Second Amendment is more important than  the First Amendment I feel sorry for you  and I think that you should come to the  conclusion that your fantasy of being a  good guy with a gun fighting a  tyrannical government is just that it's  just a fantasy if you were willing to  protest a few weeks ago you should be  willing to fight police abuse and  systemic violence out there today and  where are all of those freedom of  religion folks the the irony of what  happened yesterday is that in order to  clear out the protesters the federal  government used federal officers to  clear out the actual priest who was in  charge of st. George's Church and then  the president held out a Bible without  opening it without reading from it if  that's not blasphemy I don't know what  is why aren't you being vocal about this  abuse of religion for political ends and  where are all of the folks who claim to  care about law and order what we saw  last night was pure lawlessness just  because the federal government does it  doesn't mean that it should and it  doesn't mean that was legal and doesn't  mean that it was right if you care about  a rule of law that applies to everyone  you ought to be appalled at what  happened last night  and besides speaking out if you could  donate to the ACLU I'll put a link in  the description I would greatly  appreciate it I think there are a lot of  folks who are going to need some good  legal representation before all of this  is out and I will give to the ACLU as  well by now you've probably seen this  photo the lights were dark at the White  House last night but the lights have  been dark hit the White House for a long  time let's do what we can to bring the  light back  you
 

